---
title: "Sheet-Pan Baked Feta With Broccolini, Tomatoes and Lemon"
servings: 5
yield_verified: true
source: "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1021277-sheet-pan-baked-feta-with-broccolini-tomatoes-and-lemon"
repository: "https://github.com/nicholaswilde/recipes/blob/main/cook/main/Sheet-Pan%20Baked%20Feta%20With%20Broccolini%2C%20Tomatoes%20and%20Lemon.cook"
author: "nicholaswilde/recipes contributors"
site: "GitHub · nicholaswilde/recipes"
tags: ["approachable"]
license: "Apache-2.0"
---
Heat the oven to 400 degrees with a rack set in the lower third.

On a sheet pan, combine the @broccolini{1.25%bunch} (ends trimmed, thick stalks
split lengthwise, or broccoli, stalks trimmed and cut into bite-size pieces),
@grape tomatoes{2 1/2%c} (halved, about 2 cups), @red onion{1.25%small} (peeled,
quartered and cut into 2-inch wedges), and @lemon{0.625} (cut into thin rounds)
with the @olive oil{3.75%Tbsp} and toss.

Add @ground cumin{1 1/4%tsp} and @red-pepper flakes{5/8%tsp}, season with
@kosher salt{} and @black pepper{} (to taste), and toss again until evenly
coated.

Nestle the @feta{2.5%blocks} (6- to 8-ounce blocks, cut into 1-inch slices) into
the vegetables. (It’s OK if they break apart a little.)

Roast 15 to ~{20%minutes}, stirring halfway through but leaving the feta in
place, until the broccolini is charred at the tips, the stems are easily pierced
with a fork and the tomato skins start to blister and break down.

Serve over @cooked orzo or farro{} (for serving).

Drizzle with @olive oil{} (for serving) and serve with the remaining
@lemon{0.625} (left intact) for squeezing.

Top with @fresh basil or cilantro{10%tbsp} (leaves and fine stems, roughly
chopped, optional), if using.
